From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: three fingers switch app, four switch workspace

Three fingers sideways switched workspace, which is the gesture people
reach for to change app -- and on a machine with one workspace it did
nothing at all, which is how most people have it.

Three fingers sideways now moves between apps, in the order they were last
used, following the fingers: the app being left goes with them, the one
being gone to comes in behind it, and letting go either finishes the move
or puts everything back where it was. Four fingers sideways is workspaces.
Three fingers up is still the overview, which cannot collide with either
of them: that one is vertical.

The gestures have to be told how many fingers they are for, because "three
or more" made a four-finger swipe do both. The tracker takes a finger
count and whether it is exact, and the two sideways gestures are exact.

The finger count for workspaces is a setting, so someone who wants the old
gesture back can have it, and the defaults are written once: after that
they are the person's, and a later change of mind here does not overrule
theirs.

